    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We start by prime factorizing the radicand, which gives $2^7\\cdot3^3=2^4\\cdot2^3\\cdot3^3=2^4\\cdot(2\\cdot3)^3=2^4\\cdot6^3$.\nTaking the fourth root, we have $\\sqrt[4]{2^7\\cdot3^3}=\\sqrt[4]{2^4\\cdot6^3}=\\sqrt[4]{2^4}\\cdot\\sqrt[4]{6^3}=2\\sqrt[4]{6^3}$.\nSince $6^3=6^2\\cdot6^1=36\\cdot6$, we get $2\\sqrt[4]{6^3}=2\\sqrt[4]{36\\cdot6}=2\\sqrt[4]{36}\\sqrt[4]{6}$.\nSimplifying further, we have $2\\sqrt[4]{36}\\sqrt[4]{6}=2\\sqrt[4]{6^2}\\sqrt[4]{6}=2\\sqrt[4]{6}\\sqrt[4]{6}=2\\sqrt[4]{6^2}=\\boxed{8}$.\nThe answer is: 8",
