    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We have $\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{2^4 \\cdot 2^3 \\cdot 3^3}$.\nTaking the fourth root of $2^4$ gives us $2$, so we can rewrite the expression as\n\\[\\sqrt[4]{2 \\cdot 2^3 \\cdot 3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{2^4 \\cdot 2^3 \\cdot 3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{2^4} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2^3 \\cdot 3^3}.\\]\nSince $2^4$ has a fourth root of $2$, the expression simplifies to\n\\[2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2^3 \\cdot 3^3} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{8 \\cdot 27}.\\]\nWe can simplify the expression inside the fourth root by multiplying the numbers in the numerator and denominator:\n\\[2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{642} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 181}.\\]\nTaking the fourth root of the three twos gives us $2$, so the expression simplifies further:\n\\[2 \\cdot (2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{3 \\cdot 181}) = 4 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{543}.\\]\nThus, $a+b=4+543=\\boxed{547}$.The answer is: 547",
